A||||9||merlin||V6 Alternator removal – Need to remove tie rod?||||5||
Z||000000||merlin||06-24-2001||09:32 PM||||I’ve read several posts regarding the replacement of the alternator.  Some of the posts claim that you need to remove the tie rod, others state that you do not.  What is the correct procedure?  I have an automatic, where there’s probably less room.  Is it only automatics that need to have the tie rod removed?  In addition, what is a good brand for rebuilt alternators?   ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Mark||06-24-2001||09:54 PM||||I was able to remove and reinstall my alternator in my '86 GT 4-spd with no problems.  Just disconnect battery, remove alt/water pump belt, disconnect wire at alternator, unbolt and remove.  Maybe it's only the autos that are a bear.||||reg||1
Z||000002||terryk||06-24-2001||10:00 PM||||In the end, removing that tie-rod end makes it a billion times easier. Well, maybe not a billion, but certainly a million time. Ok, not a million, but .....||||reg||1
Z||000003||PBJ||06-24-2001||10:10 PM||||just did my wifes 86 v6 auto with a/c. removed and belt and cooling duct for back of alt and pulled it up from the top.  Did not remove any tie rod end.||||reg||1
Z||000004||cadaver||06-25-2001||02:18 AM||||I have changed mine. 86 V6 Auto without pulling the tie rod.||||reg||1
Z||000005||voyagerspe||06-25-2001||12:20 PM||||I just changed mine (again). I didnt pull the tie rod (87 gt/auto) but i did have to take the pulley off to get it out (with an impact)||||reg||1
Z||000006||87GTZ34||06-25-2001||12:28 PM||||If you have a tie rod puller it is much faster to pull it and get it out of the way. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||rogergarrison||06-25-2001||04:00 PM||||Ive change my V6 twice. 4 spd. just take off wires, cooling tube, belt and drop it rite out the bottom, I have ac too. I can change mine in 15 minutes. Takes longer to change the pully than installing it. Im not sure with an auto, but since its on the other side of car, shouldnt have any effect. I use Autozone Gold Series, lifetime guarantee and I know with all my driving and the heat in engine bay, its not gonna last prob but a couple of years. I just take em the old one, they hand me a new one, thank you very much.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 06-25-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||Ronnie||06-25-2001||05:59 PM||||Just changed mine in the Formula, V6 Auto, with no problems at all. Dropped it out the bottom. About a half hour job.<P>------------------<BR>88GT auto,88Formula T-Top,86GT 4spd<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/3fierossign.jpg"> ||||reg||6
Z||000009||filthyscarecrow||06-26-2001||12:14 AM||||just pull off the blower pipe that blows on the alt and take out the battery and you can do the whole thing from the top- even tentioning the belt. you still have to drop it ou tthe bottom though and place it back up there, but you can position it from the top. i did mine this last weekend. it still sucked because i did it last july too. damn crap parts...||||reg||1
